{"title":"2006 SMT/Geometry Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Geometry_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given a cube, determine the ratio of the volume of the octahedron formed by connecting the centers of each face of the cube to the volume of the cube.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Geometry_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/e/bbecfd0014cd02c2ae588203fe9798ab856a25d9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import three; draw((0,0,0)--(0,0,1),dotted); draw((0,0,1)--(0,1,1)); draw((0,1,1)--(0,1,0)); draw((0,0,0)--(1,0,0),dotted); draw((1,0,0)--(1,1,0)); draw((1,1,0)--(0,1,0)); draw((0,1,0)--(0,0,0),dotted); draw((1,0,0)--(1,0,1)); draw((1,0,1)--(0,0,1)); draw((1,1,0)--(1,1,1)); draw((1,1,1)--(1,0,1)); draw((1,1,1)--(0,1,1)); draw((1,0.5,0.5)--(0.5,1,0.5)); draw((0.5,1,0.5)--(0.5,0.5,1)); draw((1,0.5,0.5)--(0.5,0.5,1)); draw((1,0.5,0.5)--(0.5,0.5,0)); draw((0.5,0.5,0)--(0.5,1,0.5)); draw((0.5,0.5,0)--(0.5,0,0.5),dotted); draw((0.5,0,0.5)--(1,0.5,0.5)); draw((0.5,0.5,0)--(0,0.5,0.5),dotted); draw((0.5,0,0.5)--(0.5,0.5,1)); draw((0.5,0.5,1)--(1,0.5,1)); draw((1,0.5,1)--(1,0.5,0.5)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(0.5,0.5,1),N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(1,0.5,1),NNW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(1,0.5,0.5),SW); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"235\" />\n</p><p>Let the side length of the square be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. Consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. It's an isosceles right triangle with hypotenuse <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and legs of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/3/c5372e4a6aa030c5c2973cc7aad79bad38f9241b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{s}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"33\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/7/d77744f4a7ae0f6d26a34807139d7640fd9e29b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=\\frac{s\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"87\" height=\"41\" />, and the side length of the octahedron is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/9/e69236867c2e19e51ad90b7e34350702b471948c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{s\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"35\" height=\"41\" />. \n</p><p><br />\nNow consider the top half of the octahedron. It's a pyramid with a square base of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/9/e69236867c2e19e51ad90b7e34350702b471948c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{s\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"35\" height=\"41\" /> and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/3/c5372e4a6aa030c5c2973cc7aad79bad38f9241b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{s}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"33\" />. Therefore, its volume is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/5/295e951a2bebbb13e67627eec2cdb92f6500890c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\frac{s}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{s\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)^2=\\frac{s^3}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"170\" height=\"56\" />, and the volume of the entire octahedron is twice this, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/e/07e36890fb85cdec431c674f454f43fce1a00c96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{s^3}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"18\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nFinally, the ratio of the volume of the octahedron to the volume of the cube is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/8/5183f6b6a82621bc096c704209c1289359219d70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{s^3}{6}}{s^3}=\\boxed{\\frac{1}{6}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"69\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Geometry_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_SMT/Geometry_Problems\" title=\"2006 SMT/Geometry Problems\">2006 SMT/Geometry Problems</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017212044\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.022 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 68/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3079/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11194:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017212044 and revision id 47209. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}